IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-terms`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`

-- Tests of oa2-part2-eligibility: sections 10 and 11. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of
-- the section, with the arithmetic in the comment beside the assertion.

§ `Section 10 -- the three definitions`

-- Payment period of a month in the 2020-21 year: July 1, 2020 to June 30, 2021 (keel, s 2 "payment period" (c)).
-- Base calendar year: the last calendar year ending before that period begins: 2019 (January 1 to December 31, 2019).
`test period 2020-21` MEANS `s 10: the current payment period` (YMD 2021 2 15)
#ASSERT `test period 2020-21`'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 2020 7 1)
#ASSERT `test period 2020-21`'s `last day` EQUALS (YMD 2021 6 30)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the base calendar year` `test period 2020-21`)'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 2019 1 1)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the base calendar year` `test period 2020-21`)'s `last day` EQUALS (YMD 2019 12 31)
-- Previous payment period: the one immediately before, July 1, 2019 to June 30, 2020.
#ASSERT (`s 10: the previous payment period` `test period 2020-21`)'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 2019 7 1)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the previous payment period` `test period 2020-21`)'s `last day` EQUALS (YMD 2020 6 30)
-- The special period of April 1, 1998 to June 30, 1999 (keel, "payment period" (b)): base calendar year 1997; the
-- previous period is the fiscal year April 1, 1997 to March 31, 1998 (keel (a), fork F2).
`test period 1998-99` MEANS `s 10: the current payment period` (YMD 1998 9 1)
#ASSERT `test period 1998-99`'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 1998 4 1)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the base calendar year` `test period 1998-99`)'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 1997 1 1)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the base calendar year` `test period 1998-99`)'s `last day` EQUALS (YMD 1997 12 31)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the previous payment period` `test period 1998-99`)'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 1997 4 1)
#ASSERT (`s 10: the previous payment period` `test period 1998-99`)'s `last day` EQUALS (YMD 1998 3 31)
-- A month in the first half of a payment year (July 2021): period July 1, 2021 to June 30, 2022, base year 2020.
#ASSERT (`s 10: the base calendar year` (`s 10: the current payment period` (YMD 2021 7 1)))'s `first day` EQUALS (YMD 2020 1 1)

§ `Section 11 -- a test constructor for the facts`

-- Fields in DECLARE order:   pensioner, applied, approved, deemed(3), waived(3.1), waived(4), month of application,
--                            no pension, absent, left Canada, remained outside, not resident, ceased residing,
--                            sponsor, qualified before (8)(a), event (8)(b)
GIVEN pensioner IS A BOOLEAN
      applied IS A BOOLEAN
      approved IS A BOOLEAN
      deemed IS A BOOLEAN
      waived31 IS A BOOLEAN
      waived4 IS A BOOLEAN
      appMonth IS A DATE
      noPension IS A BOOLEAN
      absent IS A BOOLEAN
      leftCanada IS A MAYBE DATE
      remained IS A BOOLEAN
      notResident IS A BOOLEAN
      ceased IS A MAYBE DATE
      sponsor IS A BOOLEAN
      qualified IS A BOOLEAN
      event IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 11: Facts about a pensioner and a month`
`test s 11 facts` pensioner applied approved deemed waived31 waived4 appMonth noPension absent leftCanada remained notResident ceased sponsor qualified event MEANS
    `s 11: Facts about a pensioner and a month` OF pensioner, applied, approved, deemed, waived31, waived4, appMonth, noPension, absent, leftCanada, remained, notResident, ceased, sponsor, qualified, event

-- An ordinary claim: a pensioner who applied, was approved, applied in March 2024, with nothing against payment.
`test ordinary claim` MEANS `test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 11(1) and (2) -- who may be paid, and the application`

-- (1): a pensioner (s 2: application for a pension approved). Not a pensioner: not.
#ASSERT `s 11(1): a supplement may be paid to the person` `test ordinary claim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(1): a supplement may be paid to the person` (`test s 11 facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (2): applied AND approved is enough; applied alone is not; approved alone is not.
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the requirement for an application is met` `test ordinary claim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(2): the requirement for an application is met` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(2): the requirement for an application is met` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- No application and no approval, but the Minister deemed one under (3): met.
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the requirement for an application is met` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Waived under (3.1): met. Waived under (4): met.
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the requirement for an application is met` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the requirement for an application is met` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 11(3) to (3.5) -- the 65th birthday`

-- A person born on May 12, 1957 reaches 65 on May 12, 2022.
-- (3): the deemed application is dated the day the person reached 65.
#ASSERT `s 11(3): the day on which the application is deemed to have been made and approved` (YMD 1957 5 12) EQUALS (YMD 2022 5 12)
#ASSERT `s 11(3): the Minister may deem an application to have been made and approved` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3): the Minister may deem an application to have been made and approved` FALSE
-- (3.1): the Minister's satisfaction on the day of the 65th birthday is the condition of the power.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.1): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3.1): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` FALSE
-- (3.2): the duty to give written notice and the information arises when the Minister intends to waive.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.2): the Minister must notify the person in writing and provide the information` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3.2): the Minister must notify the person in writing and provide the information` FALSE
-- (3.3): "before the day on which they attain 65": the last day for the statement is the day before: May 11, 2022.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.3): the last day on which the person may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` (YMD 1957 5 12) EQUALS (YMD 2022 5 11)
-- Filed on May 11 (the last day): complied. Filed on May 12 (the birthday): not, if there are inaccuracies.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.3): the person has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` TRUE (YMD 2022 5 11) (YMD 1957 5 12)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3.3): the person has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` TRUE (YMD 2022 5 12) (YMD 1957 5 12)
-- No inaccuracies: nothing to correct, so the duty is met whenever (or if ever) a statement is filed.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.3): the person has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 1957 5 12)
-- (3.4): the person may decline "before the day on which they attain 65": May 11 in time, May 12 not.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.4): the person has declined the waiver in time` (YMD 1957 5 12) (YMD 2022 5 11)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3.4): the person has declined the waiver in time` (YMD 1957 5 12) (YMD 2022 5 12)
-- (3.5): the Minister may require an application "before the day on which the person attains 65": May 11 yes, May 12 no.
#ASSERT `s 11(3.5): the Minister may still require the person to make an application` (YMD 1957 5 12) (YMD 2022 5 11)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3.5): the Minister may still require the person to make an application` (YMD 1957 5 12) (YMD 2022 5 12)
#ASSERT `s 11(3.5): the Minister must notify the person in writing of the requirement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(3.5): the Minister must notify the person in writing of the requirement` FALSE

§ `Section 11(4) to (6) -- waiver by an earlier application, and the notices`

#ASSERT `s 11(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` FALSE
-- (5): duty only if waived under (4) AND an application is now required for a subsequent month.
#ASSERT `s 11(5): the Minister must notify the pensioner in writing that an application is required` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(5): the Minister must notify the pensioner in writing that an application is required` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(5): the Minister must notify the pensioner in writing that an application is required` FALSE TRUE
-- (5): first subsequent month September 2022: fifteen days before September 1 is August 17.
#ASSERT `s 11(5): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` (YMD 2022 9 10) EQUALS (YMD 2022 8 17)
-- (6): duty if waived under (4) AND the Minister requires an application; deadline 15 days before February 1, 2023.
#ASSERT `s 11(6): the Minister must notify the pensioner in writing that an application is required` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(6): the Minister must notify the pensioner in writing that an application is required` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(6): the Minister must notify the pensioner in writing that an application is required` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(6): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` (YMD 2023 2 20) EQUALS (YMD 2023 1 17)

§ `Section 11(7) -- the limitations`

-- (a): application in March 2024. Eleven months before March 2024 is April 2023, which may be paid; March 2023 is
-- twelve months before and may not. The earliest month is April 2023.
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(a): the month is more than eleven months before the month of the application` (YMD 2023 4 30) `test ordinary claim`
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(a): the month is more than eleven months before the month of the application` (YMD 2023 3 1) `test ordinary claim`
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(a): the earliest month for which a supplement may be paid` `test ordinary claim` EQUALS (YMD 2023 4 1)
-- (b): a month for which no pension may be paid.
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(b): no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(b): no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month` `test ordinary claim`
-- (c): left Canada in January 2023, absent throughout, remained outside. January + 6 = July 2023 is the sixth month
-- after leaving: six consecutive months, exclusive of January, end with July, so July is NOT barred; August is the
-- first barred month.
`test absent claim` MEANS `test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 20)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(c): the pensioner has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` (YMD 2023 7 15) `test absent claim`
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(c): the pensioner has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) `test absent claim`
-- Absent only part of the month: not barred. Returned in between (not remained outside): not barred. Never left: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(c): the pensioner has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 20)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(c): the pensioner has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 20)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(c): the pensioner has been outside Canada for six consecutive months before the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (d): ceased to reside on January 1, 2023, not resident throughout July 2023: six months before July 1 is January 1,
-- so the day of ceasing is "six months before the beginning of that month": barred. Ceased on January 15: not yet.
`test non-resident claim` MEANS `test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 1)) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(d): the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada six months before the beginning of the month` (YMD 2023 7 20) `test non-resident claim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(d): the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada six months before the beginning of the month` (YMD 2023 7 20) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 15)) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(d): the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada six months before the beginning of the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 15)) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Resident part of the month, or no date of ceasing: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(d): the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada six months before the beginning of the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2023 1 15)) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7)(d): the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada six months before the beginning of the month` (YMD 2023 8 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (e) and (8): a sponsor's undertaking in effect bars payment, unless (8)(a) or (8)(b).
`test sponsored claim` MEANS `test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(7)(e): an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the pensioner` `test sponsored claim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(8): paragraph 11(7)(e) does not apply` `test sponsored claim`
#ASSERT `s 11(7): a limitation bars payment of a supplement for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) `test sponsored claim`
#ASSERT NOT `s 11: a supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) `test sponsored claim`
-- (8)(a): qualified immediately before the paragraph came into force: (7)(e) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 11(8): paragraph 11(7)(e) does not apply` (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7): a limitation bars payment of a supplement for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (8)(b): an event as provided by the regulations has occurred.
#ASSERT NOT `s 11(7): a limitation bars payment of a supplement for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `Section 11 as a whole`

#ASSERT `s 11: a supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) `test ordinary claim`
-- A month twelve months before the application month: barred by (7)(a).
#ASSERT NOT `s 11: a supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` (YMD 2023 3 1) `test ordinary claim`
-- A pensioner who never applied and had no waiver: the requirement for an application is not met.
#ASSERT NOT `s 11: a supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Waived under (4) and a pension payable: payable for the month.
#ASSERT `s 11: a supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` (YMD 2024 2 1) (`test s 11 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
